k_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproductible in v4.3.stable, v4.4.beta1\n- Not reproductible in v4.0.stable, v4.2.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.3.stable (77dcf97d8) - Windows 10.0.22631 - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6614) - AMD Ryzen 9 8945HS w/ Radeon 780M Graphics (16 Threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using ctrl+k to comment multiple lines where all selected lines are empty (can have spaces or tabs) or commented and at least one line is empty and at least one line is commented, the commented lines will be correctly uncommented, but each empty line will put an error in the output.\nFor example, pressing ctrl+k when highlighting the following\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eb9a2964-fb7c-4a2f-8096-e9587be0d913)\n\nwould output\n```\nscene/gui/text_edit.cpp:3615 - Index p_from_column = -1 is out of bounds (text[p_from_line].length() + 1 = 1).\nscene/gui/text_edit.cpp:3615 - Index p_from_column = -1 is out of bounds (text[p_from_line].length() + 1 = 1).\n```\nIf any of the uncommented lines has a character other than a space or tab, every selected line gets a comment (even if already commented) and the error doesn't occurr\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Make a new script (Or open an existing script)\n2. Add a few empty lines with one having a comment\n3. Highlight all the lines and press ctrl+k\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.c